{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/pulls/892","id":4592628997,"node_id":"PR_kwDOQ8oa8s8AAAABEb31BQ","html_url":"https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/892","diff_url":"https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/892.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/892.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/issues/892","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/pulls/892/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/pulls/892/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/issues/892/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/statuses/7745ef4821f910e69420f8faee8a59b92064fd80","number":892,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"[I08:E01] Git library: bring a checkout to a named revision","user":{"login":"m2ux","id":176900785,"node_id":"U_kgDOCotKsQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176900785?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux","html_url":"https://github.com/m2ux","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nThe git library gains the operation that brings a checkout to a named revision and the run that brings a roster of checkouts to stated revisions, with a specimen that walks both against a real repository. Closes #880.\n\n## What happens today\n\nThe library materialises worktrees for branch work and derives host repositories, but nothing brings a checkout to a caller-named revision and verifies the commit landed, and a set of checkouts has no readiness construct at all.\n\n## The change\n\nThe pin operation fetches the remote, resolves the name as a tag, then a remote branch head, then a commit expression, refuses on a dirty working tree, checks out detached, and verifies the head against the resolution. It answers the commit landed and the form the name resolved as, or the refusal that left the checkout as it stood; a refusal is a value the caller reads, never an abort. A branch name pins the fetched head as one commit and the checkout does not track the branch.\n\nThe readiness run walks a roster of working-tree and revision pairs through the pin, announces each landing or refusal, and appends one entry per pin to its answer.\n\nThe git-pin-conformance specimen stands two worktrees of the host repository beneath the planning folder, names a branch, the newest tag, a commit and an unresolvable name for them, brings them there through the run, and reports what was asked beside what landed, reading the refused checkout's head back.\n\n## What was verified\n\n- The full corpus guard sweep over this branch passes, 49 guards, and the walk roster accounts for the specimen.\n- On the experiment sidecar serving this branch, the minimum viable workflow walked first, then the specimen walked to completion. The run spliced into the reference site with its prefixes composed, the pin body arrived inlined with the inherited library contract delivered once, and the four pins answered as claimed: a branch and a tag and a commit each landed as its own kind, and the unresolvable name was refused with the checkout still at the earlier pin's commit. The walk's report is the specimen's declared artifact.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nNo submodule-pointer management beyond what pinning requires; no remote-write operations.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-09-21T14:29:25Z","updated_at":"2026-10-01T12:45:54Z","closed_at":"2026-09-22T15:09:03Z","merged_at":"2026-09-22T15:09:03Z","merge_commit_sha":"f70929237452d7c7f4788d713164e1f3b3653e28","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"m2ux:workflow/880-git-revision-pin","ref":"workflow/880-git-revision-pin","repo":{"id":1137318642,"node_id":"R_kgDOQ8oa8g","name":"workflow-server","full_name":"m2ux/workflow-server","owner":{"login":"m2ux","id":176900785,"node_id":"U_kgDOCotKsQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176900785?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux","html_url":"https://github.com/m2ux","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":"A Model Context Protocol (MCP) server for AI agent workflow orchestration. Create high-fidelity, structured workflows that agents discover, navigate, and execute to fulfill user goals.","homepage":"","language":"TypeScript","visibility":"public","is_template":false,"topics":[],"forks_count":1,"forks